---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Rushabh Sanghvi writes about backend and cloud systems, AI coding tools, and practical engineering. About this personal notebook and where to find his work.">
  <div class="shell page-width">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">A little context</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Rushabh.</h1>
      <p>I work with backend and cloud systems, and write about practical engineering and AI coding tools.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>This is a home for the longer explanation: what a tool actually does, where an approach fits, and what I learned while trying it.</p>
      <p>I use concrete examples and diagrams to make the context easier to follow. When I describe a project, I try to keep its intended design separate from what I have actually tested.</p>
      <p>My earlier <a href="/series/claude-for-cloud-security/">Claude for Cloud Security</a> series lives on Medium. New writing starts here with <a href="/series/inside-an-agent-harness/">Inside Compass</a>, a series about a companion that works alongside a coding tool’s existing runtime.</p>
      <div class="about-elsewhere">
        <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
        <a class="text-link" href={site.github}>GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href={site.medium}>Medium <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/rss.xml">RSS feed <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
